\par\par \b \uc2 EXCHANGE --- The Score: The Business Week in 7 Stocks\b0\par\par\uc2 By Francesca Fontana \par \uc2 698 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 May 2022\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Corrections & Amplifications\par \par \uc2 WeWork Inc.'s stock trades under the ticker symbol WE. The Score column in Saturday's Exchange section incorrectly gave the symbol as WORK.\par \par \uc2 (WSJ May 17, 2022)\par \par \uc2 (END)\par \par \uc2 TYSON FOODS INC\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 TSN +2.2%\par \par \uc2 Tyson\uc2 's prices keep heating up. The nation's biggest meat processor by sales reported soaring second-quarter profit as the company raised prices for beef, chicken and pork. Chief Executive Officer \uc2 Donnie King\uc2  said \uc2 Tyson\uc2 's price increases are consistent with inflation, despite criticism from the White House, lawmakers and regulators that accuse the industry of using its scale to inflate Americans' food bills. \uc2 Tyson\uc2  said its cost of goods sold increased by 15% over the quarter as the company paid more for animal feed, freight and labor expenses. \uc2 Tyson\uc2  shares gained 2.2% Monday.\par \par \uc2 PELOTON INTERACTIVE INC\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 PTON -8.7%\par \par \uc2 The ride keeps getting steeper for Peloton. The once-hot stationary bike maker reported falling sales and mounting losses due to weaker demand and a return to prepandemic lifestyles. Revenue fell 24% in the quarter, marking Peloton's first year-over-year decline since going public in 2019. The company also signed a commitment letter for loans from \uc2 JPMorgan Chase & Co\uc2 . and Goldman Sachs Group Inc. Peloton last month said it would cut prices of stationary bikes and treadmills and raise monthly online workout subscriptions. Peloton shares lost 8.7% Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 WALT DISNEY CO\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 DIS +2.9%\par \par \uc2 Old-school entertainment giants are flipping the script on streaming rivals. \uc2 Walt Disney\uc2  on Thursday showed a better-than-expected quarterly jump in \uc2 Disney\uc2 + subscribers, avoiding the slowdown that dogged rival \uc2 Netflix Inc\uc2 . Meanwhile, \uc2 AMC Entertainment Holdings Inc\uc2 . reported first-quarter sales more than five times the year-ago period as moviegoers return to theaters. \uc2 Disney\uc2  shares gained 2.9% Friday.\par \par \uc2 CARVANA CO\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 CVNA -5.4%\par \par \uc2 Carvana\uc2  is downshifting. The online car dealer plans to lay off 12% of its workforce after closing a deal to expand operations that forced the company to borrow on onerous terms. In an email to employees that was reviewed by The Wall Street Journal, \uc2 Carvana\uc2  CEO \uc2 Ernie Garcia III\uc2  said that the company overshot its growth strategy and would cut around 2,500 workers, centered on its operations. \uc2 Carvana\uc2 , which offers an almost entirely online shopping and selling experience of used cars, saw a huge expansion in its business during the pandemic. \uc2 Carvana\uc2  shares declined 5.4% Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 WEWORK INC.\par \par \uc2 WE +10%\par \par \uc2 More people want space to work at WeWork. The shared-office company on Thursday said gross desk sales reached prepandemic levels amid the gradual return of employees to in-person work. The company saw lower sales during the pandemic as the Covid crisis forced many office workers to work from home and as companies reassessed their real-estate needs. In 2020, WeWork brought in new CEO \uc2 Sandeep Mathrani\uc2 , who has since refreshed operations by closing locations, renegotiating leases and cutting thousands of jobs. WeWork shares added 10% Thursday.\par \par \uc2 APPLE INC\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 AAPL -2.7%\par \par \uc2 A decline in tech stocks is gnawing at \uc2 Apple\uc2 's market dominance. State-owned oil company \uc2 Saudi Aramco\uc2 , with a capitalization close to $2.4 trillion, surpassed \uc2 Apple\uc2  as the largest company in the world by market value as of Thursday's close, according to Dow Jones Market Data. The iPhone maker is a staple investment among individual and institutional investors given its general ability to weather market storms, but investors seemed to be reassessing their love affair with the company as higher interest rates make tech stocks less attractive. \uc2 Apple\uc2  shares lost 2.7% Thursday.\par \par \uc2 TWITTER INC\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 TWTR -9.7%\par \par \uc2 A tweet from \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  raised doubts about his \uc2 Twitter\uc2  plans. The entrepreneur tweeted on Friday that his $44 billion acquisition of the social-media platform was "temporarily on hold pending details supporting calculation that spam/fake accounts do indeed represent less than 5% of users." Mr. Musk included a link to a Reuters report about a recent \uc2 Twitter\uc2  securities filing with those statistics. The \uc2 Tesla Inc\uc2 . chief executive later added that he remains committed to the deal. \uc2 Twitter\uc2  shares fell 9.7% Friday.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020220514ei5e0001t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
