\par\par \b \uc2 Business News: WeWork Narrows Loss as Desks Fill\b0\par\par\uc2 By Dean Seal \par \uc2 390 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 May 2022\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B4\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WeWork Inc.'s first-quarter loss narrowed sharply as gross desk sales reached prepandemic levels with the gradual return of employees in the U.S. to in-person work.\par \par \uc2 The shared-office company said Thursday its top line rose 28% from a year ago, with 166,000 desks sold, the highest level since the first quarter of 2020. Revenue was higher than WeWork's forecast for the period and the company raised the low end of its revenue outlook for the year.\par \par \uc2 The results are the latest sign that in-person work is slowly normalizing, after the pandemic forced many office workers to work from home and companies reassessed their real-estate needs.\par \par \uc2 WeWork, which maintains office space that it rents out to workers on a piecemeal basis, went public in October through a merger with a special-purpose acquisition company. The process came after an implosion of earlier plans for an initial public offering over corporate-governance issues and questions over its valuation.\par \par \uc2 The company also cut ties with its co-founder and former chief executive, \uc2 Adam Neumann\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The company brought in a new CEO, \uc2 Sandeep Mathrani\uc2 , who has refreshed company operations by closing locations, renegotiating leases and cutting thousands of jobs.\par \par \uc2 In the first quarter ended March 31, the reduced costs substantially cut down on the company's net loss, which came in at $435 million, or 57 cents a share, compared with a loss of $2 billion, or $14.34 a share, a year earlier.\par \par \uc2 Analysts polled by \uc2 FactSet\uc2  had been expecting a loss of 72 cents a share.\par \par \uc2 Revenue rose to $765 million in the quarter, just under Wall Street forecasts of $768 million but ahead of the company's earlier projection.\par \par \uc2 The company's total expenses fell to $1.1 billion from $2.1 billion a year earlier, aided by a $130 million gain from lease terminations.\par \par \uc2 WeWork raised the low end of its second-quarter revenue guidance to $800 million from $775 million, and upped the low end of its expected full-year revenue by $50 million to $3.4 billion.\par \par \uc2 The company said it improved its liquidity with $350 million of debt backed by \uc2 Brookfield Asset Management\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Shares of WeWork, down 58% over the past 12 months, rose about 9% on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020220513ei5d0001c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
