\par\par \b \uc2 OFF DUTY --- Gear & Gadgets: All Tied Up? --- Six cable management solutions to untangle the rat's nest on your desk\b0\par\par\uc2 By Nina Molina \par \uc2 734 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 May 2022\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par D10\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 If you work from home, and are anything like us, your desk may have begun to resemble the looping "Spaghetti Junctions" that bridge our interstates. Managing the sprawl of cables required to connect one's devices can feel as daunting as solving an infrastructure crisis. But with the bevy of handsome organizational tools now available, it doesn't need to be a bleak proposition.\par \par \uc2 Begin by restoring your desk to a more primordial state. Unplug all your devices and move them to another surface. Then, one by one and before you plug anything into a socket, arrange your items in a way that seems most functional. "When we're setting up a new desk, most of us just want to get straight to work," said Sam Beckman, who makes videos about technology for \uc2 YouTube\uc2 . But if you take the time to try several arrangements, he said, you'll eventually find the most efficient, tidiest setup. Once you've landed on a favorite and added the vital cables, consider using these management tools -- ranked here by ascending levels of neat-freakiness -- to help keep things straight.\par \par \uc2 FOR THE MILDLY BOTHERED, WITH FEW DEVICES\par \par \uc2 Wherever they originate, your cables usually lead to one of a few destinations, be that a laptop, USB hub or power brick. The Matador Re-Ties Reusable Zip Ties allow you to tightly bind all the cords on the same path so that they don't spread out and get tangled. In Mr. Beckman's view, these reusable options offer a clear advantage over more permanent solutions: If you ever want to add or move a cable, you won't need a box cutter to sever these ties open. $11, MatadorUp.com\par \par \uc2 Adhesive cable clips allow you to route your cords systematically over the surface of your desk, instead of letting them sprawl or droop wherever their whims (and gravity) might lead them. Besides black and white, the Blue Lounge CableDrops come in less basic colors such as teal, burgundy and sea foam, which makes finding a set that will match the rest of the bric-a-brac in your office easier. If you have an extra, try using it with the charger you keep at your bedside table. Set of 6, $10, BlueLounge.com\par \par \uc2 FOR THE ASPIRING, BUT REALISTIC, MINIMALIST\par \par \uc2 Even if all your cables are routed to the power strip underneath or on top of your desk in a sensible manner, they can still be a bit of an eyesore. The Yamazaki Home Cable Management Box allows you to hide the mess. The company says this also serves as a nice bit of protection from curious felines and pups who might want to undo your work. Should you need to access a plug, take advantage of your opposable thumbs to lift the top panel. $40, TheYamazakiHome.com\par \par \uc2 Upon close inspection, some entry-level desk organizers can reveal a mullet-like mien: clean on the top, messy at the back. You might be encouraged by their apparent tidiness but succumb to melancholy every time you glimpse the tangle of cables drooping underneath. The UpriteErgo Standing Desk Cable Manager provides a hammock for all these cables along the underbelly of your desk, cradling them securely off the ground. $65, UpriteErgo.com\par \par \uc2 FOR OBSESSED ORGANIZERS SEEKING A CHALLENGE\par \par \uc2 Once you've found ways to streamline how your devices connect, it is time to take matters a step further. Use one or two of the organizers from this set of elegant \uc2 Container Store\uc2  x KonMari Stackable Bamboo Drawer Organizers to corral any notebooks you want on hand while you work. Use the rest to bring order to the cables, dongles, used batteries and god knows what else you've been throwing in that neglected junk drawer. Set of 6, $35, Shop.KonMari.com\par \par \uc2 Even with your mess under the strictest control thanks to all the preceding devices, your mind can still be cluttered if your desk is your kitchen table, covered in toast crumbs. Consider upgrading to something more suitable to work, like the Herman Miller Line Storage Desk. It has big midcentury modern appeal. But like many more obviously utilitarian standing desks from startups, it also includes a nifty compartment for hiding a power strip. $2,995, Store.HermanMiller.com\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020220507ei5700009\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
