\par\par \b \uc2 Business News: \uc2 UAW\uc2  Walks Off Job At CNH Industrial\b0\par\par\uc2 By Bob Tita \par \uc2 394 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 May 2022\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Workers at \uc2 CNH Industrial NV\uc2  walked off their jobs Monday for the first time in nearly 20 years after their union and the farm and construction equipment manufacturer failed to reach an agreement on a new contract.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2 -represented employees' contract with \uc2 CNH\uc2 , which is based in London, expired early Sunday, but the two sides kept negotiations going through Sunday and into Monday morning. The union said it broke off the talks Monday afternoon and instructed workers to leave their jobs.\par \par \uc2 Neither the union nor the company provided specifics about the terms under discussion.\par \par \uc2 "CNH Industrial is disappointed that the parties were unable to reach an agreement," the company said in a written statement. "We remain committed to reaching an agreement, and we are working to resolve this issue."\par \par \uc2 "Our members at \uc2 CNH\uc2  strike for the ability to earn a decent living, retire with dignity and establish fair work rules," said \uc2 Chuck Browning\uc2 , director of the \uc2 UAW\uc2 's agricultural implement department.\par \par \uc2 The strike at \uc2 CNH\uc2  involves about 1,100 workers at the company's plants in Racine, Wis., where its farm tractors are built, and Burlington, Iowa, where construction machinery is assembled.\par \par \uc2 The action is the latest in a series of strikes at large U.S. companies where unions have pushed for higher wages and better benefits amid rising inflation, a tight labor market and rising corporate profits.\par \par \uc2 In March, more than 500 California refinery workers went on strike at \uc2 Chevron Corp\uc2 . following a contract negotiation stalemate. Manufacturing workers at \uc2 Kellogg Co\uc2 . and Volvo last year went on strike, seeking higher pay.\par \par \uc2 CNH\uc2 , brands of which include CaseIH and New Holland farm machinery and Case construction equipment, is a competitor for \uc2 Deere & Co\uc2 ., where 10,000 \uc2 UAW\uc2  members walked off their jobs last fall for more than a month before approving a new six-year contract.\par \par \uc2 After approving the contract in November, \uc2 Deere\uc2  workers received an immediate 10% raise and each worker received an $8,500 bonus. Additional 5% pay raises will be provided to \uc2 Deere\uc2  workers in two other years, and lump-sum bonuses amounting to 3% of workers' annual pay will be awarded in the three other years.\par \par \uc2 The auto workers union's strike against \uc2 CNH\uc2  is the first at the company since late 2004, the company said.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020220503ei530001b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
