\par\par \b \uc2 MANSION --- Annotated Room: Classic Meets Contemporary --- This work-from-home space in Los Angeles mixes modern pieces with traditional design\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Hine \par \uc2 492 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 April 2022\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par M8\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Even before the pandemic made home offices a priority, this newly built, 12,000-square-foot house in the Holmby Hills neighborhood of Los Angeles included a dedicated work-from-home space.\par \par \uc2 The homeowners, who were in their 30s and parents to both a toddler and a baby when the project started three years ago, wanted to blend his more traditional aesthetic with her interest in contemporary art and design. "We put a youthful spin on the study by incorporating a contemporary rug and playing with modern artwork," says designer Kara Smith, founder of KES Studio in L.A. "We wanted it to feel young and unexpected."\par \par \uc2 To channel the husband's more classic tastes, the design incorporated extensive millwork and bookcases. "The ceilings are incredibly high, but we needed to be mindful of the scale," Ms. Smith says. "We aligned the tops of the bookshelves with the window line then created a dramatic molding that continues onto the ceiling."\par \par \uc2 On the open wall near the desk, Ms. Smith and the wife looked for a work by a contemporary artist that had a simple neutral aesthetic. They landed on an ink and colored pencil drawing by Jonas Wood that the husband calls, "a home run."\par \par \uc2 Here are some of the home office's design elements.\par \par \uc2 1. The desk, by Dakota Jackson, is made from hand-polished elm burl and finished with a custom gray stain. It has a leather inset top. Ms. Smith calls it the ultimate executive desk. // Price: Price: $47,976\par \par \uc2 2. The chair had to be comfortable, but because it's so visible, Ms. Smith also wanted it to be great looking. The Poltrona Frau leather chair designed by Jean-Marie Massaud fit both criteria. // Price: $5,397\par \par \uc2 3. Throughout the house, Ms. Smith focused on finding pieces that felt collected versus designed; the Jean-Louis Deniot Helios chandelier, "looks like something you found and fell in love with," she said. // Price: Price: $15,513\par \par \uc2 4. Ms. Smith commissioned Kyle Bunting to create the custom hair-on-hide rug. "There are a lot of hard surfaces in the room so we wanted a giant rug," she says. "We spent a lot of time working with Kyle on the hide colors and on the pattern." // Price: $17,939\par \par \uc2 5. The mohair-covered custom chairs (based on vintage originals) work for a meeting, but Ms. Smith notes that right now, at least, they are mostly used by the husband as a comfortable place to read. // Price for the pair: $14,535\par \par \uc2 6. JRC Group constructed the extensive crown molding, wainscoting and bookcases in the office. According to Ms. Smith, it took about 17 samples to finalize the combination of wood species, sheen and color for the custom work. // Price: $85,000\par \par \uc2 (See accompanying photo -- WSJ Apr. 15, 2022)\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020220415ei4f00007\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
