\par\par \b \uc2 U.S. News: Pact Will End Minneapolis Teacher Strike\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sara Randazzo \par \uc2 353 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 March 2022\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par A3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Teachers and education support professionals in Minneapolis reached a tentative deal Friday with the city's school district to end a strike there that closed schools for 2 1/2 weeks.\par \par \uc2 Talks to reach an agreement stretched deep into the night, with Minneapolis Public Schools announcing at 4 a.m. that school should be back in session Monday.\par \par \uc2 Around 28,500 students have been out of school since March 8 as about 4,500 teachers and other educators picketed over wages, hiring, class sizes and more resources for mental-health support.\par \par \uc2 Terms of the new deal weren't announced, but the Minneapolis Federation of Teachers and Education Support Professionals said in a Friday morning statement that "major gains were made on pay for education support professionals, protections for educators of color, class size caps and mental health supports."\par \par \uc2 The union is expected to vote on the deal in the coming days.\par \par \uc2 The district's superintendent, Ed Graff, called the strike and resolution "a life-changing experience for all of us" in a statement. He said the classroom time lost during the strike could be made up for by adding minutes to the school day, extending the year, or holding school on scheduled days off.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this past week, the district had said its best offer to the teachers included starting salaries of more than $50,000, a full-time social worker in every school, a 20% wage increase for coaches and other concessions.\par \par \uc2 As school districts across the country face staffing shortages and teacher burnout from the pandemic, unions have gained some leverage in talks with management.\par \par \uc2 In Sacramento, a strike by 4,600 teachers and school workers entered its third day Friday. Teachers there said they are pushing for better health benefits and changes that will help fill 250 teacher vacancies and 400 classified support roles.\par \par \uc2 The Sacramento City Teachers Association said no talks have been scheduled yet with the district.\par \par \uc2 Another teachers strike in a smaller district in California's Sonoma County wine region lasted six days this month.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020220326ei3q0002z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
