\par\par \b \uc2 Demand, Pricing Spur General Mills to Raise Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 By Will Feuer \par \uc2 611 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 March 2022\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 General Mills Inc\uc2 . raised its fiscal 2022 outlook, saying it expects recent price increases to help offset cost pressures and demand for its packaged-food brands to remain strong even as the pandemic wanes.\par \par \uc2 The maker of Cheerios and Betty Crocker cake mix said supply-chain challenges and rising costs have held back business, but consumer demand for food at home is still above pre-pandemic levels as many people continue to work from home. Recent price increases are helping offset supply issues, the company said.\par \par \uc2 In the company's fiscal third quarter ended Feb. 27, \uc2 General Mills\uc2 ' North American retail segment saw sales rise 1% to $2.81 billion from a year earlier. The company said sales growth in the latest quarter was constrained by supply shortages in certain categories. But compared with the same period in 2019, before the pandemic, organic sales were up 6% in the latest quarter.\par \par \uc2 For the full fiscal year, \uc2 General Mills\uc2  said it expects organic net sales to rise by 5%, in part thanks to higher pricing. The company previously said it expected a 4% to 5% increase in sales.\par \par \uc2 General Mills\uc2  said constant-currency adjusted earnings are expected to be flat or up to 2% higher. The company previously said it expected adjusted earnings to be between 2% lower and 1% higher. The company reiterated its expectation of input cost inflation of 8% to 9% and significant costs related to supply-chain disruptions.\par \par \uc2 The company said an increase in the pet population during the pandemic and the premiumization of pet food are expected to help drive higher sales. \uc2 General Mills\uc2 ' pet segment saw sales jump 30% to $568 million in the latest quarter.\par \par \uc2 Shares of \uc2 General Mills\uc2  closed on Wednesday at $64.23, up 2.5%. The stock is down 4.7% so far this year.\par \par \uc2 As with other consumer packaged-goods companies, \uc2 General Mills\uc2  benefited from a surge in demand for groceries at the start of the pandemic as homebound Americans spent more time cooking and baking.\par \par \uc2 But now, the company is grappling with supply-chain challenges, higher raw-material costs and labor shortages that in recent quarters have hurt its ability to fully deliver on customer orders.\par \par \uc2 In response to higher costs and supply-chain challenges, \uc2 General Mills\uc2  and rivals like \uc2 Campbell Soup Co\uc2 . and \uc2 Conagra Brands Inc\uc2 . have opted to raise prices. That has contributed to higher grocery bills for consumers, with the \uc2 U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics\uc2  reporting in February that prices for all food consumed at home rose 8.6% over the past 12 months, the biggest one-year increase since April 1981.\par \par \uc2 General Mills\uc2  has been raising prices for its products through a variety of measures, including list price increases and changing packaging and sizes to charge more for an ounce.\par \par \uc2 The company has also worked to secure alternative supply sources and boosted its inventory levels for certain raw materials in an effort to control costs, according to executives.\par \par \uc2 Overall, the Minneapolis, Minn., company posted a fiscal third-quarter profit of $660.3 million, up from $595.7 million in the year-earlier period.\par \par \uc2 On a per-share basis, the company earned $1.08 a share, compared with 96 cents a share a year earlier.\par \par \uc2 Adjusted for divestitures and other one-time items, the company posted earnings of 84 cents a share.\par \par \uc2 Analysts surveyed by \uc2 FactSet\uc2  were looking for 78 cents a share.\par \par \uc2 Quarterly sales rose slightly to $4.54 billion from $4.52 billion a year earlier.\par \par \uc2 Analysts surveyed by \uc2 FactSet\uc2  expected the company to report sales of $4.55 billion for the quarter.\par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw553\pich341\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal8295\pichgoal5115
