\par\par \b \uc2 Contract Impasse Leads to Strike At Chevron Refinery in California\b0\par\par\uc2 By Allison Prang \par \uc2 343 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 March 2022\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 More than 500 \uc2 Chevron Corp\uc2 . employees went on strike at a refinery in California on Monday amid a contract stalemate.\par \par \uc2 The strike comes after the company's contract with the United Steelworkers Local 5 union expired Feb. 1, according to the \uc2 United Steelworkers\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Union members at the Bay Area plant had been working on a rolling extension ahead of the strike.\par \par \uc2 "USW members continued to report for work throughout the pandemic so our nation could meet its energy needs," said Mike Smith, chair of the \uc2 United Steelworkers\uc2 ' National Oil Bargaining Program. "They deserve a fair contract that reflects their sacrifice."\par \par \uc2 The Richmond refinery has about 3,000 total employees, according to \uc2 Chevron\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The company said the contract it is offering workers is competitive, fair and responsive to the union's concerns.\par \par \uc2 "We have negotiated in good faith for months, reaching two tentative agreements that were rejected by the union, and we are ready to continue discussions with USW so we can reach an equitable agreement," \uc2 Chevron\uc2  said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The strike comes amid surging gasoline prices across the U.S.\par \par \uc2 In California, the average price of regular unleaded gasoline is at $5.855 a gallon, the highest in the country, according to AAA.\par \par \uc2 Chevron\uc2  said it is prepared to continue its normal operations and doesn't expect supply-chain problems. It wouldn't say whether gas prices would be affected.\par \par \uc2 The broader \uc2 United Steelworkers\uc2  reached a pattern agreement with the oil industry about a month ago, but the individual units bargain over local issues as well, according to the union.\par \par \uc2 Chevron\uc2  said United Steelworkers Local 5's demands were more than what the company considers reasonable and went beyond the national pattern bargaining agreement.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Chevron\uc2  strike is the latest in a string of high-profile strikes that have swept the country over the past several months.\par \par \uc2 Workers at \uc2 Deere & Co\uc2 ., \uc2 Mondelez International Inc\uc2 . and \uc2 Kellogg Co\uc2 . ended up accepting new contracts that included pay raises, among other provisions.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020220322ei3m0000r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
