\par\par \b \uc2 U.S. News: IRS Plans Hiring in Bid to End Backlog\b0\par\par\uc2 By Richard Rubin \par \uc2 584 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 March 2022\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par A4\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON -- The \uc2 Internal Revenue Service\uc2  plans to hire 5,000 employees over the next few months and 5,000 more by the end of September 2023, aiming to eliminate a long backlog of unprocessed tax returns and correspondence that has left millions of frustrated taxpayers in its wake.\par \par \uc2 The agency's goal is to take a paperwork pile that sits at around 20 million items and reduce it to about one million by the end of the year, senior Treasury Department officials said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The hiring binge will start with job fairs in Kansas City, Mo., Austin, Texas and Ogden, Utah, between now and April 1, concentrating new workers at \uc2 IRS\uc2  facilities in those cities that process incoming paperwork and in jobs that require minimal training.\par \par \uc2 Using exceptions to normal federal hiring rules, the \uc2 IRS\uc2  expects to be able to get people working, on site, within 45 days instead of four to six months, avoiding delays that can lead applicants to take other jobs instead of waiting for the government. Pay rates for the positions would vary. Federal workers earn a minimum wage of $15 an hour.\par \par \uc2 IRS\uc2  officials have also struggled to hire new employees, contending that the government can't compete with companies such as \uc2 Amazon.com Inc\uc2 . for lower-wage workers and that the federal hiring process takes too long. Officials hope the special exceptions will improve that hiring rate.\par \par \uc2 "We are leaving no stone unturned -- taking an all-hands-on-deck approach to ensure as many employees as possible are dedicating time to return processing," said \uc2 IRS\uc2  Commissioner \uc2 Charles Rettig\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The agency is also trying to automate more of its processes so it doesn't require as many people or as much paper correspondence as it does now.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 IRS\uc2  got behind on paperwork when employees were sent home from government buildings early in the pandemic, and it has struggled to catch up even as many workers returned to on-site jobs. Those difficulties have been compounded by new pandemic-era programs such as stimulus payments, advance child tax credits and employee retention tax credits, all of which run through the agency and require staff and resources.\par \par \uc2 Still, electronic filing has been running smoothly and 2021 tax refunds are flowing in advance of the April 18 deadline for most taxpayers, the agency said. But paper tax returns and written correspondence can take months to get processed, and any discrepancies between what taxpayers file and information in government records can be cumbersome to resolve.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 IRS\uc2  has about 75,000 employees, so 10,000 marks a significant jump, though some will be temporary workers or backfill for employees who are retiring or leaving.\par \par \uc2 As of March 4, the \uc2 IRS\uc2  had 7.2 million unprocessed individual tax returns, plus even more unprocessed employment-tax returns and amended tax returns. Some measures put the total backlog above 20 million pieces.\par \par \uc2 That all means many people are still waiting for their refunds from tax year 2020, to the point where the \uc2 IRS\uc2  has been issuing special reminders of how to do electronic filing for 2021 when the 2020 return isn't processed. Restaurants have been warning the government about cash-flow crunches because of the slow pace of employee-retention tax credit payments.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 IRS\uc2  has suspended some automated notices to taxpayers and shifted some employees into positions that help them reduce the backlogs and is continuing those efforts.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020220311ei3b0001g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
