\par\par \b \uc2 U.S. News: Big Federal Projects to Require a Labor Deal\b0\par\par\uc2 By Andrew Restuccia and David Harrison \par \uc2 368 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 February 2022\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par A3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON -- President Biden signed an executive order mandating that the government enter into agreements with labor unions setting pay and conditions for federal construction projects that cost more than $35 million.\par \par \uc2 The White House said the wider use of project labor agreements would ease coordination challenges on large construction projects, and raise wages and training standards for workers.\par \par \uc2 "The executive order I'm going to sign today is going to help ensure that we build a better America, we build it on time and we build it cheaper than it would have been otherwise," Mr. Biden said Friday at an iron workers union hall in Upper Marlboro, Md.\par \par \uc2 Under a project labor agreement, the government or a general contractor negotiates with one or more labor unions to set terms of a project before the project starts. The agreement can cover everything from pay, workplace conditions or worker qualifications.\par \par \uc2 For the government, a project labor agreement can make a project run more smoothly since many of the possible conflicts get ironed out ahead of time, proponents say. Critics say they can sometimes make projects more expensive.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden's order, which applies to federal procurement, will cover $262 billion in federal government construction contracts and affect nearly 200,000 workers, according to the White House.\par \par \uc2 The federal government is about to embark on billions of dollars in construction projects following the enactment in November of a roughly $1 trillion infrastructure bill.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden has put his support for unions at the center of his domestic policy agenda. He regularly appears at events with union officials, publicly endorsed a union drive by \uc2 Amazon.com Inc\uc2 . workers in Alabama, and pushed for pro-union provisions in the infrastructure package.\par \par \uc2 Unions are a key political constituency for Mr. Biden. Union members helped him win in several Rust Belt states in the 2020 election and will be crucial in the coming midterms. While most contributions to political campaigns from unions in recent cycles have gone to Democrats, some rank-and-file union members in the building and trade industries have gravitated toward former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020220205ei250002c\par }\par \b \uc2 Search Summary\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Date\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/2021 to 01/01/2026\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl